{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Load the supplied HR LDIF data into LDAP on node1 and retain the supplied records under /srv/legacy2/ldap-attribute-privacy.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The supplied employee entry was added on node1 and the final database contains Morgan Lake, mail, and employeeNumber values matching the LDIF. The original 201-byte hr.ldif remains at the required path with its original mode and timestamp and survived node1's restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-440e66eee1a94909","cmd-b2122c87bb6142c3","cmd-68afc1957c6642d8","cmd-ff0bbd2aa7aa46ea"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Allow the directory-reader identity to search employee names and mail addresses remotely from node2 while withholding employeeNumber.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Authenticated searches from node2 returned Morgan Lake and morgan@hr.test without employeeNumber, both before and after both node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a530a41708284c1c","cmd-b95b3e11c4084863","cmd-e967e27b6ede4cff","cmd-e055e6ec0bdd4756"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Ensure only the HR administrator can read or change employeeNumber.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The administrator read employeeNumber and successfully changed it, while the reader's modification was rejected with insufficient access and left the value unchanged. The administrator restored HR-4815, and the final ACL grants administrator write access while denying all others.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a530a41708284c1c","cmd-3774aa3bbb754c11","cmd-9a1e35609a00469b","cmd-ff0bbd2aa7aa46ea"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Prevent anonymous users from seeing employee records.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Anonymous subtree searches from node2 returned no employee entries before and after the restart sequence; the final ACL also denies non-reader access to the HR subtree.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a530a41708284c1c","cmd-e967e27b6ede4cff","cmd-ff0bbd2aa7aa46ea"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Provision dedicated demonstration credentials for the reader and HR administrator.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Dedicated directory-reader and hr-admin identities were configured. Root-only credential files were present on both nodes, and the node2 credentials successfully authenticated as each identity before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-92868bd7b33c46f5","cmd-b2122c87bb6142c3","cmd-7256a412e3804fe3","cmd-b95b3e11c4084863","cmd-e967e27b6ede4cff","cmd-ff0bbd2aa7aa46ea"]},{"id":"R6","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on Ubuntu 7.10 with kernel 2.6.22-14-generic. OpenLDAP/ldap-utils 2.3.35 packages from the legacy Ubuntu repositories were installed and remained functional after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b0a7be93db794e57","cmd-5a47f93795ff4f6c","cmd-ff0bbd2aa7aa46ea","cmd-e055e6ec0bdd4756","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_prepare:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Package-index updates and LDAP package installation established required prerequisites; configuration, credential, and data writes directly implemented the requested service; the temporary administrator modification was a bounded behavioral test and was restored in the same command; temporary password and LDIF files were removed; and both reboots implemented the mandatory restart protocol. Failed SSH checks and the timed-out LDAP inspection were read-only observations. Final lifecycle snapshots show no temporary-file residue or package inconsistency attributable to the executor.","evidence_ids":["cmd-93e487d08c4447bd","cmd-060f2ad142824c37","cmd-b0a7be93db794e57","cmd-5a47f93795ff4f6c","cmd-92868bd7b33c46f5","cmd-b2122c87bb6142c3","cmd-9a1e35609a00469b","cmd-734c440a3e534db2","cmd-01b21affc3c5499f","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart observation, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity independently corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered service, data, credentials, and access-control behavior.","limitations":["The final hr.ldif checksum uses MD5 while the preparation baseline uses SHA-256, so unchanged content is supported by matching size, mode, timestamp, the read-only command history, and successful post-restart data checks rather than a directly comparable final hash.","The legacy platform does not support the lifecycle collector's systemd failed-unit check, and its generic listening-socket snapshot did not expose slapd; service recovery is instead directly demonstrated by pid/socket checks and successful LDAP operations.","Credential secrets were appropriately redacted. Node1's credential file is therefore evidenced by existence and root-only permissions, while successful authenticated operations directly validate the provisioned identities and node2 credential files."]}
